</pre>
3. K-Nearest Neighbor (KNN): KNN is a non-parametric algorithm that is used for classification and regression tasks. It works by finding the k-nearest labeled instances in the dataset and using them to make a prediction.
Here is a code snippet to demonstrate the usage of KNN in Java:
