    "sentence": "John gave Mary a book.",
    "voice": "active",
    "direct_object": "book",
    "indirect_object": "Mary",
    "preposition": "to",
    "pronoun": null
}
```
Note that the program may not work perfectly for all sentences, as natural language processing is a complex and ongoing research area. However, this example should give you a good starting point for analyzing sentence structures in Python.

