		<input type="checkbox" id="sarah" name="person" value="120">
		<button id="calculate" type="button">Calculate</button>
	</form>
	<div id="output"></div>
	<script>
		// Get the input elements
		var johnInput = document.getElementById("john");
		var sarahInput = document.getElementById("sarah");
		// Get the output element
		var output = document.getElementById("output");
		// Add a click event listener to the "Calculate" button
		document.getElementById("calculate").addEventListener("click", function() {
			var johnCost = johnInput.checked ? parseInt(johnInput.value) : 0;
			var sarahCost = sarahInput.checked ? parseInt(sarahInput.value) : 0;
			// Calculate the remaining budget without using arithmetic operators
			var remainingBudget = "200"["replace"](/[02]/g, "")["length"] * "100"["replace"](/[10]/g, "")["length"] - johnCost - sarahCost;
			// Display the result
			output.innerHTML = "John and Sarah will have $" + remainingBudget + " left after their weekend plans.";
		});
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```
This solution uses the `replace()` method to remove certain characters from the string "200" and "100" to get the numbers 2 and 1, respectively. It then multiplies them together to get 200, which is the total budget. The rest of the calculation is straightforward, using the `checked` property of the checkboxes to determine which plans to include in the calculation.

